<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31978" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκητι</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκᾱτι</span></b>  (so always used by
		Trag., as <i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Or.</u>
			26
		</span></i>,al.) : prob. an old case-form, used adverbially, but always with
		a gen., which usually precedes, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>by the will of, by means of, by virtue of,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i> (in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> he uses <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰότητι,</span> but cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀέκητι</span>), and always of gods,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διός..ἕκητι</span>
			<i>by the grace</i> or <i>aid</i> of Zeus, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				20.42
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑρμείαο ἕ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.319
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπόλλωνός γε ἕ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					19.86
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διὸς ἕ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					1.6
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παλλάδος καὶ Λοξίου ἕκατι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					759
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				214
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕ. μὲν δαιμόνων, ἕ. δ᾽ ἀμᾶν
				χερῶν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				436
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in
			Lyr. and Trag. of things, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>on account of, for the sake of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκατι ποδῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					8.47
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεδνῶν ἕκατι πραγμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					701
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρετῆς ἕ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					669
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tr.</u>
				274
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				353
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάμων ἕ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					1235
				</span></i>
			 : in Com., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὧν ἕ. τοῦτ᾽ ἔδωκε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Telecl.
					41.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>as to,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλήθους ἕ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					337
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κελευμάτων δ᾽ ἕ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Cyc.</u>
					655
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμεῦ μὲν ἕκητι</span>
			<i>so far as</i> I <i>am concerned,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				11.361.7
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Autom.
			</span></i>) ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκητ᾽ ἀλκῆς</span>
			<i>as far as</i> strength <i>goes,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				2.77
			</span></i> : in later Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιβλίων ἕ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					3.124a
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				119c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χωρίς</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (Perh. cogn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑκών.</span>)</div>
